  "summary": {
   "status": "complete",
   "text": "In a March 2026 Senate opening statement, Raman said that if confirmed he would help NIST deliver on the President’s AI action plan and maximize innovation across the American AI tech stack, including semiconductors, quantum, biotechnology, and advanced manufacturing. In the same statement, he described a vision for NIST focused on accelerating technology innovation through industry partnerships, championing trusted technology standards globally, and speeding adoption by American industry. In 2024 reported statements from Purdue, he cited an urgent need for AI-equipped sensor networks to detect and identify threats and noted the Institute of Chips and AI among Purdue programs focused on physical AI. In August 2026 as NIST Director, Raman said NIST’s contribution to the Genesis Mission reflected its commitment to U.S. leadership in critical technologies and that NIST was using public-private partnerships to apply advanced AI to manufacturing and cybersecurity.",
   "sids": [
    "s1",
    "s7",
    "s6",
    "s2",
    "s3",
    "s4",
    "s5"
   ],
